> If it isn't too much trouble, could you create a single comprehensive 
dictionary file for it (instead of the 20 or so included in the zip on 
Lojban.org)? =D
I won't do that.
First of all, I sometimes update jbovlaste dsl dictionary as jbovlaste is 
being continuously updated.
Secondly, if while using GoldenDict I don't want to look at let's say 
etymology I simply release the corresponding icon in the dictionary toolbar 
(in this case it's the button with the word "xa").
As for the other dictionaries the same logic applies. Sometimes i don't want 
to look at noralujv definitions, sometimes I hate jbo.wikipedia.org 
dictionary as I haven't been able to export it correctly ;-).
If all GoldenDict dictionaries are merged together how shall we determine 
the source of any given definition ?
Is it so difficult to simply unpack the whole zip file into GoldenDict 
folder ?

>Oh. Are people actually using quickdict? I kind of stopped development on 
it cuz it felt like it was at least stable enough that I wasn't embarrassed 
with it.

> But if people are actively using it then I would probably be much more 
motivated to keep newer/better versions coming. Maybe an option for "input 
format" so the jbovlaste xml export can be used.
I currently use GD. But it doesn't have lujvo auto-splitting functionality. 
QD should be developed.

> I use GoldenDict, personally. However, the most recent dictionaries kinda 
broke it.
What do you mean ? What version of GD ? What operating system ? Which 
dictionary is broken ?

